# Date Format YYYY/MM/DD Test

Evaluate this before opening the file (or set it in your init file):

    (setq altodo-date-format "%Y/%m/%d")

Then run `M-x revert-buffer` and check that the dates below get the date faces
and that the filters `due-date:` / `start-date:` of the sidebar work with them.
The same dates written as YYYY-MM-DD are plain text with this setting.


## Slash Dates

[ ] Starts 2099/01/01 ->
[ ] Due -> 2099/12/31
[ ] Range 2099/01/01 -> 2099/12/31
[ ] Overdue -> 2000/01/01
[ ] Started 2000/01/01 -> 2099/12/31


## Hyphen Dates (not dates with this setting)

[ ] Starts 2099-01-01 ->
[ ] Due -> 2099-12-31
